hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16753","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother, from Umm Uthman daughter of Sufyan, and she is the mother of the elder sons of Shayba; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman said: and she had pledged the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Shayba and he opened; when he entered the House and returned and finished, and Shayba returned, there was a messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to answer; so he came to him and said: I saw a horn in the House, so conceal it; Mansur said: Abd Allah ibn Musafi narrated to me, from my mother, from Umm Uthman daughter of Sufyan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him in the hadith: It should not be in the House anything that distracts those praying."
